The wasting fever is a sickness found in [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/index|Oresk]]. It works on the soul: a healthy soul is a bundle of cloth, and a fevered one rots like a sack left in the rain, its threads coming apart until more than half is gone. Those it takes are thin to the point of starving, in pain, burned by sunlight and shy of it, and only half awake.

[[People/Althane/Henrik|Henrik]] holds it for a mild form of [[Phenomena/Althane/Sanguis Noxa|vampirism]], and its sufferers for lesser nightkin. The [[Org/Althane/Golden Sparrows|Sparrows]] found the early cases gathering around one freshwater well and sealed it, but new ones keep appearing across the city, and the [[Org/Althane/The First House|First House]] is said not to want a cure. Henrik now holds that the fever is noxblood in the food: the House has been seeding the city's food with a dilute noxblood that builds up in whoever eats it. Drawing the divine energy back out of an infected person's blood cures them, and Henrik has done it.

He has since broken the fever in Oresk, drawing the noxblood out of the sick one at a time.
